/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Buildroot output and pinned upstream checkout
/buildroot/output/
/buildroot/dl/
/buildroot-upstream/
# Buildroot builds out-of-tree here. `output/` is the default; the CPU-baseline work
# added `output-corei7/` and `output-generic/` as two isolated trees, and one careless
# `git add -A` staged 672,911 files out of the first of them. A build directory is not
# a thing to enumerate by name every time somebody makes another one.
#
# Root-anchored and directory-only: `/output*/` matches output/, output-corei7/ and
# output-generic/ at the top of the repository, and nothing nested that merely has the
# word in its name.
/output*/

# Build artifacts
*.img
# What tools/make-preview-release.sh assembles: a 194 MB asset, its checksums and its
# notes. The notes are generated from the commit and the build, so committing them would
# be committing a copy that goes stale the moment either moves.
/release/
*.img.xz
# QMP screendumps land in QEMU's cwd, which is wherever it was launched from.
*.ppm
*.erofs
*.efi
*.verity

# Signing material must never be committed
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

# Agent working directory, including worktrees of this repository
/.claude/

# There is no Node in this project: no build step, no test runner, nothing served. The
# tests that check the console page's script parse it with whatever engine is on PATH and
# skip when there is none, which is the only reason `node` is ever mentioned. A
# package.json, a lock file and a node_modules/ were committed here once, by a mistyped
# `npm install` in the repository root, and sat in a public tree for a week. Root-anchored
# and directory-only, in the style of `/output*/` above.
/node_modules/
